  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "myeid_new_file",
    "file": "opensc/src/pkcs15init/pkcs15-myeid.c",
    "description": "`myeid_new_file` copies the profile application-DF path into `file->path` and unconditionally appends a two-byte FID at lines 420-421 without checking that `p->len + 2 <= SC_MAX_PATH_SIZE`. With a 16-byte path, the first append writes past `sc_path.value[16]` into the adjacent `len` field and corrupts it; subsequent path operations become out-of-bounds. In this PoV, `myeid_create_key` later trusts the corrupted `file->path.len` in `memcpy(path->value, file->path.value, file->path.len)`, overflowing the private-key info and corrupting its trailing `aux_data` pointer. Error cleanup then dereferences that wild pointer in `sc_aux_data_free`, where the crash is observed.",
    "conditions": "The fuzz input is parsed as a MyEID PKCS#15-init profile and supplies an application-DF path of exactly `SC_MAX_PATH_SIZE` (16 bytes; PoV path `3402807431768F2defa66A0851478479`). The harness binds the profile/card and invokes EC key generation. MyEID key creation calls `myeid_new_file`, which attempts to append a two-byte key-file identifier to the already-full path. The resulting corrupted path length is propagated to `myeid_create_key`'s unchecked copy into `sc_pkcs15_prkey_info.path`; when key generation subsequently fails and frees the partially created object, the corrupted `aux_data` pointer causes the wild read."
  },
